      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ensuring data security is crucial. Technically, you can start by implementing strong encryption for data in transit and at rest, using secure protocols such as HTTPS, and regularly updating your software to protect against vulnerabilities. On an organizational level, establishing clear data protection policies, conducting regular security training for anyone who has access to the data, and keeping a log of who accesses the data can help prevent unauthorized use. Additionally, consider using a reputable third-party service to store and process customer data rather than handling it all in-house. If a breach is detected, have a prepared plan for how you will notify affected parties efficiently, as required by GDPR. Keeping your systems and procedures up-to-date and being proactive about implementing security best practices will significantly reduce the risk of unauthorized access or data leaks.",
