      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To detect hidden threats, focus on intrusion detection and prevention systems (IDPS) to monitor for suspicious activities. Regularly conduct security audits and vulnerability assessments to identify and fix potential weaknesses. Consider implementing a robust access control system with the principle of least privilege, where users only have access to what they need to perform their job functions. Whistleblower policies can help uncover issues that your IT team might not detect; ensure employees are aware that they're encouraged to report any suspicious activity. Employing security information and event management (SIEM) systems can help with real-time analysis of security alerts generated by applications and network hardware. Additionally, conducting frequent training alongside encouraging a culture of security mindfulness can lead to higher chances of early detection. Constant vigilance, combined with the appropriate technological tools and a well-informed team, can greatly reduce the risk of hidden threats.",
